  "assessment": "All 51 exact-target rows reconciled: sixteen direct generators, twenty-three supporting curricular topics, five illustrative examples and seven conditional outcomes. The closest owns three generators, computational AI owns four, cognitive processes/language owns six, and responsible/explainable AI owns three. Split the last coherent ethical-design direction from the original omnibus cognitive/responsible candidate. It is recorded separately as maximum-reached, without claiming an unconstructed fourth curriculum is feasible.",
  "sourceSupport": {
    "9685–9700": "Current official programme and curriculum directly discuss machine intelligence, human brain/cognition, learning, language, HCI/robotics, ethical/sustainable/human-centred and explainable systems. Emotion interpretation and brain interfaces are motivating human-process questions, not guarantees of an entire BCI or affective-computing course. HCI/Autonomous Systems, Cognitive Neuroscience, Computational Linguistics, Hybrid Intelligence and Ethics catalogue content corroborates their specific academic contexts.",
    "9701–9723": "Dated catalogue entries corroborate the curricular topics. Software Engineering, AI for Nature and Environment and Methods for Responsible AI appear in the optional CSAI menu; they support legitimate programme interests without being falsely counted as compulsory exchange-path subjects.",
