  "candidateReassessment": {
    "Computational AI & autonomous systems": "Substantial implementations in algorithms/software, numerical modelling, learning, vision, robotics and reinforcement learning directly respond to this cluster; formal systems and database courses have specific computational roles.",
    "Cognitive processes, language & neuroscience": "Neuropsychology, perception, higher cognition, psycholinguistics and social cognition supply the core; philosophy of mind/agency, evidence synthesis and stylistic interpretation change its research priorities. Computing and mathematics remain substantial. No full HCI, emotion-recognition engine, BCI laboratory or NLP formation is asserted.",
    "Responsible and explainable AI": "Ethical theory, technological responsibility, transparency and human-centred evaluation form one coherent additional direction. Ethics is already present in all three accepted programmes; mind/agency reflection adds to the cognitive option. Dedicated explainability engineering, sustainable-AI modelling and interface design remain gaps. The three-programme maximum stops construction, rather than a false no-match or blanket rejection."
